      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='98770' id='895' param='horz' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98934' x='533' y='615'>
            <zone h='98770' id='24' type-v2='layout-basic' w='98934' x='533' y='615'>
              <zone h='88155' id='7' param='horz' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98934' x='533' y='11230'>
                <zone h='88155' id='5' type-v2='layout-basic' w='98934' x='533' y='11230'>
                  <zone h='33916' id='78' name='Final View (2)' w='98934' x='533' y='57537'>
                    <zone-style>
                      <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                      <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                      <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                      <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    </zone-style>
                  </zone>
                  <zone forceUpdate='true' h='7932' id='111' type-v2='text' w='98934' x='533' y='91453'>
                    <formatted-text>
                      <run bold='true' fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='8'>*Please take into account following statements to avoid confussion or mistaken calculations:</run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='8'>1. Metrics such ASP, Avg Qty per Cat, or Frequency are isolated meaning that for example for ASP, Total GPV of only an specific category is taken, divided by the total orders of this specific category. </run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='8'>2. If you sum KPIs such Total Orders per category you will NOT come to the total orders of a country/region, because you will be duplicating data.</run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='8'>3. Avg L1 Cat metric is correct from an L1 Level View</run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='8'>4. Total Avg Listed SKUs are the same for L0, L1, and L2 contrywise. However, if you start adding countries or regions, L0, L1 and L2 avg. listed SKUs may differ, since there are categories that are not present on all countries. </run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='8'>5. </run>
                      <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='8' italic='true'>% Avg Listed SKUs from Total</run>
                      <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='8'> and </run>
                      <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='8' italic='true'>% GPV from Total</run>
                      <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='8'> on the table metrics and bar chart will display the correct information ONLY if there is no filter on M.C. Zero or M.C. One Categories. </run>
                    </formatted-text>
                    <zone-style>
                      <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                      <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                      <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                      <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    </zone-style>
                  </zone>
                  <zone h='41461' id='236' name='% Listed SKUs vs % GPV (2)' w='85729' x='533' y='11230'>
